content.thinking:
Excellent report. One real bug found: in commitStep, the snapshot is taken AFTER setting finished=true, so the recovery point stores post-commit state — restoring to RP-1 doesn't un-commit S4. Fix: take snapshot BEFORE marking finished.

```js
function commitStep(stepId) {
  const s = stepById(stepId);
  if (!isOpen(s) || !checksAllDone(s)) return;
  if (s.irreversible) {
    state.seq += 1;
    const snapshot = structuredClone({ done: state.done, completedAt: state.completedAt });  // BEFORE finish
    state.done[stepId].finished = true;
    state.checkpoints.push({...});
    ...
  } else {
    state.done[stepId].finished = true;
    ...
  }
}
```

Wait — snapshot must be taken before `state.done[stepId].finished = true`. But `structuredClone` of state.done done before the mutation. Restructure:

```js
function commitStep(stepId) {
  const s = stepById(stepId);
  if (!isOpen(s) || !checksAllDone(s)) return;
  let rp = null;
  if (s.irreversible) {
    state.seq += 1;
    const snapshot = structuredClone({ done: state.done, completedAt: state.completedAt });
    rp = { id: "RP-" + state.seq, seq: state.seq, stepId: s.id, stepName: s.name, actionLabel: s.actionLabel, at: now(), snapshot, superseded: false };
  }
  state.done[stepId].finished = true;
  if (rp) {
    state.checkpoints.push(rp);
    log("commit", `已通过确认门提交「${s.name}」（口令 ${s.passcode}）· 自动创建恢复点 ${rp.id}`);
    toast(`已提交：${s.name} · 恢复点 ${rp.id} 已创建`, "violet");
  } else {
    log("check", `已完成可逆步骤「${s.name}」（${s.actionLabel}）`);
    toast(`已完成：${s.name}`);
  }
  ...
}
```

Also there's a knock-on: after recovery, restoring to RP-1 puts S4 un-finished, but RP-1 remains. Then re-commit creates RP-2 for S4; old RP-1 stays non-superseded pointing at same step — that's fine semantically (both are restore points; RP-1 is "before first migration attempt", RP-2 "before second"). Hmm, slight semantic redundancy but acceptable. Actually cleaner: on restore, mark the restored checkpoint itself superseded too? If you restore TO RP-x, then RP-x represents the state you're now in — keeping it usable is fine (re-restore = no-op-ish). Keep.

Also fix the minor meta duplication: `.st-meta` showed "已提交 · 不可逆 · 不可逆" — because ST_TEXT["committed"] = "已提交 · 不可逆" and then we append "· 不可逆" for irreversible. Fix: ST_TEXT committed = "已提交"; and keep the appended "· 不可逆".

Also the knock-on deviation in the test (S5→RP-2 etc.) was caused by the bug; after fix, scenario works as originally planned.

Apply both fixes, then have the same agent re-run the harness (SendMessage) to regenerate evidence — especially 04/06 with the corrected sequence (RP numbering will shift back to plan). The harness re-run will overwrite PNGs and log. Ask to also re-assert the recovery expectations (S4 un-committed after restore, badges 确认门 0/3).

Then write README.md, then Prax validate.

